name o4-01-bvr-headon-1
timeout 600

# CAMPAIGN O4, SORTIE 1 OF 10 — GAF MiG-29G AGAINST THE F-16, the DACT evaluations of JG 73 "Steinhoff"
# at Laage, 1991-2003 (doc/campaigns/o4-gaf-mig29g-dact.md). This is the ONE campaign in the set in which
# both FlightBox airframes really flew against each other, in the configuration modelled, in the period
# named, and its anchor is itself a measurement exercise: ~450 sorties against the F-16 alone.
#
# THE ARENA, and every number in it is [SET]: a block of Baltic airspace centred 55.20 N 13.60 E, about
# 145 km north-north-east of Laage (53.92 N 12.28 E, [T4]) and west of Bornholm. It is over water, which
# is why the campaign is flown with `--elev const` (0 m = sea level is the TRUTH here, not an
# approximation) and why the two range targets are moored hulks rather than pits. The hulks are `hulkwest`
# (12.60 E, behind the F-16's entry) and `hulkeast` (14.60 E, behind the MiG's): each side's briefed run
# is to the OTHER side's hulk, so neither jet is merely drifting toward a merge. Campaign rule 3 —
# a fight with nothing on the ground has no reason to be where it is.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: does the head-on BVR baseline REPRODUCE on the campaign's own arena and its
# own loadout? doc/duels.md row 1 measured a draw at 46.90 N with 2 AIM-120 against 2 R-27R; this file
# re-asks it 8 degrees further north, over water, with the full air-superiority racks (4 AIM-120 + 2
# AIM-9 against 2 R-27R + 4 R-73) that the campaign's magazine carry needs. A different answer here is
# a finding about the arena, not about the jets.
#
# THE LOADOUT IS DECLARED IN FIRING ORDER, and that is doc/duels.md D4 rather than a pylon map: weapon
# selection is not a decision either pilot can make (FBCommandTarget::WeaponSelect is NotImplemented on
# both modules), so the SMS steps through the occupied stations in ascending order and the mission has to
# put the radar rounds on the low stations. The MiG's 2x R-27R inboard + 4x R-73 outboard IS the
# canonical 9-12 load; the F-16's 4+2 is real, its station assignment is the tree's convention.
#
# THE MAGAZINE IS CARRIED. Sorties 1, 2 and 3 are flown by the SAME two airframes (`viper`/`fulcrum`) and
# the campaign carries `stores`: what this sortie fires is gone from the next one. That is the whole
# point of sortie 3 and it is stated there.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-29, `--elev const`, standalone AND as campaign step 1 — identical): the SENSOR and
# TRIGGER half reproduces doc/duels.md row 1 to within a rounding error — viper detects at t=24.0 /
# 52.19 nm against fulcrum's t=108.2 / 25.41 nm, shots at 9.56 nm (Rtr 9.79) and 10.07 nm (Rtr 10.26)
# against the published 9.57/9.78 and 10.02/10.25. The OUTCOME does not: this file exits 0, an F-16 kill
# at t=549.8. The first AIM-120 arrives 6.54 m out and only degrades, both jets fly on, they re-merge,
# and at t=540 the F-16 still has AMRAAM on the rails where duel-headon's two-round rack had none. Its
# second round arrives 2.23 m out. THE DRAW IN duel-headon WAS A MAGAZINE, and this file is the
# measurement that says so. The MiG fires 1 of its 2 R-27R, which is what feeds sortie 2's carry.
#
# READING RULE: the exit code is NOT the verdict, and this file is the reason the campaign says so.
# duel-headon's reading rule predicts exit 3 with both alive, because both pilots ship with the same
# doctrine (designate at the airframe's lock range, release at Rtr), the two Rtrs sit within half a mile
# of each other and the FIRST round from either side then arrives outside its warhead's lethal radius.
# All of that holds here and the run still exits 0. Read, in this order: eng_detect_s / eng_shot_s /
# eng_shot_nm / eng_shot_rtr_nm (they must match doc/duels.md row 1 — if they do not, the ARENA moved and
# the campaign has a different problem), then the DETONATION lines and WHEN the second one is fired.
# exit 2 (a physical K.O. of a healthy jet) would be a defect.

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 55.20000 12.72600 8000 90.0 450       # 111.0 km apart, co-altitude, head-on, both outside both
  set gear up                                 # radar gates at t=0 so both runs begin with a real search
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink off                            # a duel is fought on own sensors
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim120                          # firing order: four radar rounds, then the two IR rounds
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60                           # ALE-47, 60/60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 55.20000 14.60000 8000 450               # the briefed run: hulkeast, the MiG's own range target
  objective kill unit fulcrum
  objective survive

unit fulcrum
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 55.20000 14.47400 8000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad                           # the wide non-locking search pattern
  set n019_range_nm 27                        # the set's own documented search reach
  set n019_emission illum                     # LOUD from t=0, as duel-headon's baseline is
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r                            # firing order: the two inboard radar rounds first
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set store 1 r73
  set store 2 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30                           # BVP-30-26, 30/30 — half the F-16's magazine
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 55.20000 12.60000 8000 450               # the briefed run: hulkwest, the F-16's own range target
  objective kill unit viper
  objective survive

unit hulkwest
  module target_soft                          # range hulk, moored at the block's west end [SET]
  team friendly
  spawn 55.20000 12.60000 ground 90.0 0

unit hulkeast
  module target_soft                          # range hulk, moored at the block's east end [SET]
  team hostile
  spawn 55.20000 14.60000 ground 270.0 0
